    <string name="bt_disclaimer">An entry is worked out at the open of the candle after the signal, not at that candle\'s close. A position still open on the last candle is closed there, so the equity curve ends on a number that could really have been taken. What happened is no guarantee of what will.</string>
    <string name="bt_sharpe_note">The Sharpe penalises movement upward as heavily as movement downward, so a rule with a few big wins scores worse than a listless one. The Sortino measures only the losing side and becomes large and meaningless when there are few losing candles — which is exactly where it is most often quoted.</string>
    <string name="bt_with_shorts">With shorts</string>
    <string name="bt_shorts_note">Shorting is approximate: both sides\' fees are counted, but a borrow rate and a funding rate are not in a candle series.</string>
